{"book":5,"chapter":16,"context":{"chapter":16,"title":"Three Pilgrim Feasts","summary":"Israel is to keep Passover, the Feast of Weeks and the Feast of Tabernacles at the place God chooses. The chapter then turns to appointing judges and doing justice.","background":"Three times a year every man was to appear at the sanctuary (v. 16). Passover, first kept in homes in Egypt, is here kept at the central place (vv. 5–6). Tabernacles was a week-long autumn harvest feast when people lived in booths (Leviticus 23:42). The city gate, where judges sat (v. 18), served as the town's court.","customs":[{"term":"Month of Abib","verses":"16:1","note":"Abib, meaning young ears of grain, fell in early spring (March–April). It was later called Nisan."},{"term":"Feast of weeks","verses":"16:9-10","note":"Seven weeks after the start of grain harvest. Greek-speaking Jews called it Pentecost ('fiftieth'), the feast at which the Spirit came in Acts 2."}],"watchFor":["The household, servants, Levite, stranger, orphan and widow all share the feasts (vv. 11, 14).","'Bread of affliction' links eating to remembering (v. 3).","The Hebrew of v. 20 says 'justice, justice': KJV 'that which is altogether just.'"],"connections":["Exodus 12:14-20","Leviticus 23:15-21","Acts 2:1","John 7:2"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["שָׁמוֹר","shamor","H8104","HVqaa","keep"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["חֹדֶשׁ","chodesh","H2320","HNcmsc","[the] month of"],["הָאָבִיב","ha'aviv","H24","HTd/Ntbsa","<the> Abib"],["וְעָשִׂיתָ","ve'asita","H6213","Hc/Vqq2ms","and you will observe"],["פֶּסַח","pesach","H6453","HNtmsa","a passover"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["אֱלֹהֶיךָ","'eloheikha","H430","HNcmpc/Sp2ms","God your"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","for"],["בְּחֹדֶשׁ","bechodesh","H2320","HR/Ncmsc","in [the] month of"],["הָאָבִיב","ha'aviv","H24","HTd/Ntbsa","<the> Abib"],["הוֹצִיאֲךָ","hotzi'akha","H3318","HVhp3ms/Sp2ms","he brought out you"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֱלֹהֶ